+//! A contact of the stripe's blend on face F that ends at a vertex V of the
+//! edge E between F and the blend's other face Fo (the blend thinner there
+//! than V's tolerance: it comes to nothing at V), on another edge of F
+//! across which a face Fn goes on tangentially from F, Fn meeting Fo along
+//! an edge from V (the spine goes on there): the contact ends on E at V as
+//! well (a vertex interference on E with the contact's transition), so that
+//! the blend cuts E from F.
+void ChFi3d_OwnEdgesAtVertices(const occ::handle<ChFiDS_Stripe>& CorDat,
+                               TopOpeBRepDS_DataStructure&       DStr,
+                               const ChFiDS_Map&                 VEMap,
+                               const ChFiDS_Map&                 EFMap);
